  "instrument": "TMA1995",
  "kind": "section",
  "number": "62",
  "ref": "TMA1995/s62",
  "text": "The registration of a trade mark may be opposed on any of the following grounds: (a) that the application, or a document filed in support of the application, was amended contrary to this Act; (b) that the Registrar accepted the application for registration on the basis of evidence or representations that were false in material particulars. Note: For file see section 6.",
